@startuml senku-sorted-run-levels
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
top to bottom direction

title Senku Shard Maintenance and Sorted-Run Levels

artifact "mergeFanIn committed flush generations\nEach contains shards S000 ... S(m-1)" as Flushes
component "Shard-parallel maintenance\n\nCreate one job per shard\nMerge configured fan-in\nFold duplicate keys" as InitialMerge

frame "Level 0: one sorted run per shard and maintenance batch" {
  folder "shard-00000/level-00000/run-00001/\nmanifest.properties + ordered chunk parts" as L0S0
  folder "shard-00001/level-00000/run-00001/\nmanifest.properties + ordered chunk parts" as L0S1
  artifact "..." as L0More
  folder "shard-(m-1)/level-00000/run-00001/\nmanifest.properties + ordered chunk parts" as L0Sm
}

frame "Recursive promotion for shard S001" {
  artifact "mergeFanIn level-0 sorted runs\nshard S001 only" as NL0
  component "Merge configured fan-in" as MergeL0
  folder "one logical level-1 sorted run\nshard-00001/level-00001/run-00001/\nmanifest.properties + ordered chunk parts" as L1

  artifact "mergeFanIn level-1 sorted runs\nshard S001 only" as NL1
  component "Merge configured fan-in" as MergeL1
  folder "one logical level-2 sorted run\nshard-00001/level-00002/run-00001/\nmanifest.properties + ordered chunk parts" as L2
}

Flushes --> InitialMerge
InitialMerge --> L0S0
InitialMerge --> L0S1
InitialMerge --> L0More
InitialMerge --> L0Sm

L0S1 --> NL0 : maintenance batches accumulate
NL0 --> MergeL0
MergeL0 --> L1
L1 --> NL1 : level-1 runs accumulate
NL1 --> MergeL1
MergeL1 --> L2
L2 --> L2 : repeat for higher levels

note right of L1
The same hierarchy exists independently
for every shard. Normal maintenance merges
only the same shard and level. finishWriting()
keeps that rule, permits partial same-level groups,
and rewrites a lone lower run one level upward
when a higher run still exists. It never directly
merges different numeric levels. Terminal numeric
levels may differ between shards.
The maintenance worker still publishes an empty output run
with partCount=0, recordCount=0, and no data part.
end note
@enduml
